      "title": "Walmart permits autonomous AI shopping agents with review and spending limits",
      "summary": "Walmart announced it will allow AI agents to shop on its website starting next month. The platform will introduce controls enabling customers to set spending limits and review or approve purchases before transactions complete.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Launches next month on Walmart's website for customer AI agents.",
        "Includes controls to set spending limits on agent purchases.",
        "Requires systems for customers to review and approve transactions."
      ],
      "design_implication": "Designing checkout has always assumed a human carefully reviewing a cart before paying. When autonomous agents make purchases on a customer's behalf, design shifts from multi-step checkout funnels to pre-transaction permission boundaries and asynchronous transaction approvals. Start mapping spending threshold controls and explicit approval modals into checkout settings, establishing clear safeguards before autonomous buyers place automated orders.",
